WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.003
-We are in the worst stage
of the pandemic so far,

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:07.373
and the outgoing president is
laser-focused on two things --

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:09.041
overturning the election results

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:11.878
and counter-programming
Joe Biden's inauguration.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:14.313
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:18.217 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:21.287
Until Trump emerged for his
unhinged rally in Georgia

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:22.822
this weekend, the nation
was watching

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:25.858
a bizarre split screen
where on one side,

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:27.660
you had the incoming president,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.729
who doesn't actually have
any power yet,

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.664
addressing the nation
on a regular basis,

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.967
consulting his team of medical
advisers, laying out his plans,

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:37.337
and calling for action amid
the worst national crisis

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.705
in a hundred years,
and on the other side,

00:00:39.705 --> 00:00:41.307
you had the current president

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:44.043
in a sort of self-imposed
hibernation

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:46.212
from which he emerged
only rarely

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.814
to give bizarre minute-long
press conferences

00:00:48.814 --> 00:00:52.218
about the stock market
or lumber around his golf course

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:55.655
by himself like a hungover
Bigfoot on vacation.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:58.524
[ As Trump ] No pictures.
No pictures, please.

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:00.260
[ Normal voice ] And not only
has he been avoiding

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.861
public appearances,
he's apparently

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.663
avoiding private ones, too.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.431
Amid the worst stage
of the pandemic,

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:07.500
with the country setting new
records for cases,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.301
hospitalizations, and deaths,

00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:12.138
Trump has been ignoring his own
COVID task force.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.373
-The task force will remain
together,

00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:17.010
though of course a question is
how often they're going to

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.011
continue to meet with
the Vice President.

00:01:19.011 --> 00:01:21.347
They've been trying to resume
their weekly schedule

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.949
they had maintained before
the election,

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:25.718
but our reporting still shows
President Trump himself

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:28.521
has still not attended
a coronavirus task force meeting

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.356
in months.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.825
-I mean,
obviously he should be there.

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:35.094
But it is a little like Hawkeye

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.796
not showing up
to an Avengers meeting.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:39.232
They can probably go ahead
and start without him.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.467
You know what? I'm just going to
put him down for arrows,

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:44.303
and if I'm wrong, we can change
it when he shows up.

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:46.572
Obviously it would be ideal to
have a president who, you know,

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:49.007
cares that thousands of
Americans are dying every day.

00:01:49.007 --> 00:01:51.544
But I have to imagine it might
also be a bit of a relief

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:54.180
to the members of the task force
when Trump doesn't show up

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.582
to distract everybody
with dumb questions.

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:58.084
"As you'll see here,
Mr. President,

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:59.418
the virus is now spiking

00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:01.521
in almost every region
of the country.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.856
[ As Trump ] Uh, yeah,
just spitballing here --

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:07.627
is it possible it spiked
in a way that could have

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:10.129
led to voter fraud in say --

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:12.431
again, this is just off
the top of my head --

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:13.933
Nevada, Pennsylvania, Michigan,
and Georgia?

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.034
[ Normal voice ]
"I'm sorry, Mr. President,

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.068
how would that even happen?"

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:18.170
[ As Trump ]
It's a spitball, guys.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:20.172
You can't ask follow-ups
to the spitballs.

00:02:20.172 --> 00:02:22.241
It's like the first rule
of spitballs.

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:25.211
Because then you're
deincentivizing the spitballs.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.813
[ Normal voice ] Of course,
if he had showed up

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.414
to any of those meetings,
he would have heard

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:32.251
dire warnings like this from one
of his own medical advisers.

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:35.120
-This is not just the worst
public health event.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:38.591
This is the worst event
that this country will face,

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.860
not just from a public health
side.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.563
-Yeah. 2020 is one of
the [bleep] years on record,

00:02:44.563 --> 00:02:47.333
and it's ending in the [bleep]
possible way.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.802
Which, I guess, is exactly
what you'd expect.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.639
You don't watch "Paul Blart"
hoping it's going to turn into

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:54.673
"Citizen Kane" in the third act.

00:02:54.673 --> 00:02:56.709
[ Gruff voice ] They didn't have
Mankz writing the script!

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.911
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:00.446
[ Normal voice ] We could have
easily been prepared for this.

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.248
Instead, we have to hope
our current president

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.484
is sitting at home in his
sweatpants channel surfing

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:07.219
and accidentally clicking past
"Meet the Press"

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:09.655
on his way to watching,
I don't know, an episode

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:11.791
of "Ghost Hunters,"
hoping they find one

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:12.925
who voted for Biden.

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:14.860
Because Trump doesn't listen
to his advisers.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.829
Instead, Trump prefers
to get his information

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:19.999
about the pandemic from medical
experts like this guy.

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.468
-I have the best analogy
which I hope makes sense.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.603
-Okay, ohh, let me stop you
right there.

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:26.506
If you have the best analogy,

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:29.808
you shouldn't have to hope
it makes sense.

00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:33.046
Then again, you shouldn't be on
TV if you can't tie your shoes

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.980
without doing
the whole rabbit story out loud.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.016
But go on,
let's hear this analogy.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.350
-Pete Rose is going through
a divorce

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:40.085
in the '70s, and it was brutal.

00:03:40.085 --> 00:03:42.154
It was on the front pages
of every headline.

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:44.623
They said, "Pete,
you are hitting .360

00:03:44.623 --> 00:03:46.959
while you're going through this
public divorce. It's brutal."

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:50.159
And he said, "I would rather
go through a divorce

